{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>A new wife.</b> Who is new to him, even a widow — excluding one who takes back his divorcee (Sifrei; Sotah 44)." "<b>And shall not pass over him.</b> A matter of the army." "<b>For any matter</b> that is a need of the army — not to supply water and food, and not to prepare the roads. But those who return from the battle lines by the word of the priest — such as one who built a house and did not dedicate it, or betrothed a woman and did not take her — they supply water and food and prepare the roads (there)." "<b>He shall be to his house.</b> Also for the sake of his house: if he built a house and dedicated it, or if he planted a vineyard and redeemed it, he does not move from his house for the needs of the war." "<b>He shall be.</b> To include his vineyard." "<b>His house.</b> This is his actual house." "<b>And make glad.</b> He shall make his wife rejoice. As the Targum renders: ״וְיַחְדֵי יָת אִתְּתֵהּ״. And whoever translates it as ״וְיֶחְדֵּי עִם אִתְּתֵהּ״ is mistaken, for that is not the translation of וְשִׂמַּח (Piel — 'make glad') but of וְשָׂמַח (Qal — 'was glad')."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:15.344619239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}